::  name       mantra line fields equality gate
::  shape      count - int (@u32) -> lawful - int (@u32)
::  invariant  answers 1 exactly when count is line fields=6; answers 0 otherwise
::  law        mantra/src/weave.rye Line.fields exact
::  example    6 -> 1 - 5 -> 0 - 7 -> 0
::  readers    Mantra - Glow Tend a1 unfinished - Ashvini
::  nib        equinox-e256-equality-fifth-v0 - STOA337
::
::  Ashvini equality - fifth pedestal gth cannot speak. The sur shape names
::  a weave Line's six fields (text - gen - pos - site - run - ord); this gate
::  decides *exactly*, not by a ceiling.
::
::  Moved three to four on 20260907.094747, the lap that bound this constant
::  to the Rye. Line grew `site` when identity became a pair, and this gate
::  went on answering 0 for the count its own subject carries, green the whole
::  time, because nothing compared it against mantra/src/weave.rye.
::
::  Moved four to five on 20260907.182409, when Line grew `run` and document
::  order left LineId for Place. The binding held this time: the constant scan
::  refused on the lap the field arrived, which is what the elder note was
::  written to buy.
::
::  Moved five to six on 20260916.024500, when Line grew `ord` -- the order key
::  asked apart from the identity, so a replacement can inherit where a line sat
::  without inheriting who it was (REDS %680, on Keaton's word). The binding
::  held a second time, and on the same lap the field arrived.
|=  sample=@u32
?:  (eq sample 6)  1  0
